       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe and may be a mistake.\n\n**The problem:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to **6400 mg/day**.\n- The usual maximum single dose of oral ibuprofen is **800 mg**.\n- The usual maximum daily dose for adults, including prescription anti-inflammatory dosing, is **3200 mg/day**.\n\nThis order is twice both limits. At this dose there's a high risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury and other NSAID toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?**\n- **400 mg four times daily** (1600 mg/day total). The 1600 might be the daily total rather than the per-dose amount.\n- **800 mg three or four times daily** (2400\u20133200 mg/day), the upper end of anti-inflammatory dosing.\n- Something else?\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it. If 1600 mg per dose really is intended, please confirm and give the clinical reason. I'd also recommend a pharmacist review before I enter it."
      }
