      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this one, even with your confirmation. 6400 mg/day isn't a borderline dose. No adult indication supports it, and it's twice the maximum in standard references. Giving it four times a day would carry a serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and other toxicity. You didn't give a clinical reason, so I can't treat it as a deliberate exception rather than a unit or transcription error. An order like this should go through a pharmacist and your hospital's override process, not a plain entry from me.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Change the dose.** I can enter right away, for example:\n   - **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3200 mg/day, the labeled maximum), or\n   - **400 mg by mouth four times daily** (1600 mg/day).\n2. **Keep the dose.** If you have a specific reason for 1600 mg per dose, please involve the on-call pharmacist and record the reason through your institution's high-dose override process. That keeps the documentation and safety checks in place.\n3. **Different goal.** If the issue is pain or inflammation that isn't controlled at maximum ibuprofen dosing, I can help you consider other options, such as adding scheduled acetaminophen or switching drugs.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
